@ dup 'line 128 -trailing                       \ type the current line with its number                                     rot 2 u.r space type cr ;                                                                           head-                                                                                                                           : _caret    ( -- )          col @ 3 + spaces [char] ^ emit cr ;                 \ mark the cursor under the line                : _upd      ( -- )          update save-buffers ;                               \ save the edit; QUIT empties the buffers       -->                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( Block editor 2/3 ____________________________________________ 10/11/26 BNE )                                                  : _len0     ( ca u -- ca n ) >r 0  begin dup r@ xor while                       \ n = chars before the first NUL, at most u                                 2dup chars+ @ 0= if r> drop exit then  1+           \ stop at the end of a terminal line                                        repeat  r> drop ;                                                                                   : _src      ( -- ca )       blk @ if blk @ block 8 bit exit then TIB ;          \ address of the input source                   : _rest     ( -- ca u )     _src >in @ chars+  >in @ 128 + -128 and             \ parse the rest of the line                                                dup >in @ - swap >in !  _len0 -trailing ;                                                           : _gap      ( n -- ca n' )  remain min  dup remain swap - >r  'cursor swap          \ open n blank chars at the cursor                                      2dup chars+ >r over r> r> cmove>  2dup blank ;     \ shift the rest of the line right               : _cut      ( n -- )        remain min  dup remain swap - >r  'cursor               \ delete n chars at the cursor                                          2dup swap chars+ over r> cmove                      \ shift the rest of the line left                                           over remain swap - chars+ swap blank ;              \ blank the end of the line                     : _ins      ( ca u -- )     dup _gap rot drop  dup col +!  cmove ;              \ insert text at the cursor and move past it    : _put      ( ca u -- )     row @ 'line dup 128 blank  swap 128 min cmove ;    \ make text the current line                     : _fbuf     ( -- ca )       fbuf 8 bit ;                                        \ address of the find string                    : _same     ( ca1 ca2 u -- flag ) for  over @ over @ xor                        \ true if u chars at ca1 and ca2 match                                      if 2drop r> drop 0 exit then                        \ a difference: no match                                                    1 chars+ swap 1 chars+ swap  next  2drop -1 ;                                                       : _at       ( pos -- flag ) dup 127 and #fbuf @ + 128 u<= if    